cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Aegis in academic or published work, please cite it as below."
title: "Aegis: a reproducible runtime for testing what agent tool isolation actually guarantees"
abstract: >-
  Aegis is a research instrument for secure agent tool execution. Every tool
  call walks a fixed enforcement pipeline — policy evaluation, capability
  resolution, sandboxed execution — with audit wrapping all three, so that
  denials, traps, resource-cap trips, and panics all produce records. It
  distinguishes two trust models explicitly: Model A, where tool logic runs
  inside a wasmtime WebAssembly component with cap-std filesystem scoping and
  per-call resource ceilings, and Model B, where the effect runs in host Rust
  and receives a capability check and an audit record but no sandbox
  isolation. The project's purpose is to make isolation claims falsifiable
  rather than assumed: it ships a threat model with named non-goals, an
  adversarial test suite, hash-chained signed audit records with a documented
  wire format, and benchmarks reported with hardware and toolchain
  attribution.
type: software
